  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Proverbs 6:27**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Island Garden Song**: back after 109 archived shows (2891 days) [3]\n- **The Day the Aliens Came**: rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- **Going to Mexico**: back after 48 archived shows (1241 days); rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Hello Sarah**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Sign of the Crow 2**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Ox Baker Triumphant**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Alpha Desperation March**: back after 63 archived shows (1372 days); rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2009-03-21.aud.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 23 songs; 80 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Microphones lost contact with the recorder briefly during the song's climax [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Cassettes/Going to Mexico, Ox Baker Triumphant, Stalling for time/Sign of the Crow 2, Surrounded, Tuning/The Day the Aliens Came, [Moon Colony Bloodbath [1]\n- The performer engaged in excellent banter with the audience [2]\n- The first song became an Amazon.com bonus track for the unreleased album [1]\n- The setlist offered a great mix of old and new songs [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2009-03-21.aud.flac16**: taped by Thomas J Hartnett; transferred by Thomas J Hartnett; source: AUD [1]. Also: John Vanderslice performed a solo show on the 2009 Gone Primitive tour [1]",
